## CWE rule
CWE-401 — Missing Release of Memory after Effective Lifetime (Memory Leak)
Description: Memory or another allocated resource is not released on all paths, causing exhaustion over time.
Vulnerability indicators:
- Error paths that exit without freeing what was allocated
- Reassigning a pointer without freeing its previous value
Safe patterns:
- A single exit point with cleanup (goto cleanup)
- Automatic resource management (RAII, smart pointers)

